    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Pakistan became the first Muslim country to achieve chapter status in the Sigma Theta Tau International (STTI) global network, when on Saturday, September 9, 2000, Aga Khan University School of Nursing Honor Society (AKUSON-HS) received its Charter. STTI is an international honor society, with more than a quarter of a million members representing 83 countries. It has 406 chapters in colleges and universities in the United States, Canada, China, South Korea, Taiwan and Australia.",
